1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Hello everyone, today we are going to talk about the little techniques to add fonts in colou.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,000
First, import a .dxf file.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:16,000
In the pop-up window, select the option to convert to font.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:23,000
This can help you convert the font information in the .dxf file to the font in colou.

5
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:28,000
After opening, you can see the font information displayed in the window.

6
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:31,000
If there is no normal display font in your window,

7
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:36,000
you can find the display font in the 2D window display menu.

8
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Open the display settings and you can see the normal display font.

9
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Then let's check the font information of the sleeve version on the right.

10
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:48,000
For the fonts that are not correctly identified,

11
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:53,000
we can add and correct them in colou.

12
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:57,000
First, let's add the saved font of the sleeve.

13
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:02,000
You can find the font tool in the 2D tool bar.

14
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Then, click once to add the font.

15
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:09,000
You can add the font on the two outside pages.

16
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:11,000
In the property editor,

17
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:13,000
you can modify the font type,

18
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:17,000
width and seam type.

19
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Then let's first deal with the sleeve page,

20
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:24,000
the cross point connection method at the top.

21
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Select this section of the font,

22
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:26,000
we can find it in the property editor.

23
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:28,000
In the property editor,

24
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:30,000
set the cross point as the second type.

25
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:34,000
Let's see the connection effect of the six types of fonts.

26
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:37,000
You can adjust it according to the actual craftsmanship.

27
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:58,000
Next, let's create an uneven width of the seam.

28
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:00,000
First, select this page line.

29
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:02,000
In the property editor,

30
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:04,000
change the seam type to point.

31
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:07,000
Then we can set the two ends of a line

32
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:10,000
for different seam widths.

33
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:12,000
The default is the line type.

34
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:14,000
The whole seam is the effect of uniform width.

35
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:17,000
The translation in the software will be updated later.

36
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:20,000
We can follow the arrow direction in the 2D window.

37
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:22,000
The effect is the same as in the 2D window.

38
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:24,000
The effect is the same as in the 2D window.

39
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:26,000
The effect is the same as in the 2D window.

40
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:30,000
Change the width of the end to 10 mm.

41
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:31,000
On the other side,

42
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:39,000
we can change the width of the seam to the correct 10 mm.

43
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:43,000
Similarly, we can edit the opening width of the seam.

44
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:46,000
So we can modify the seam.

